# 🧠 Machine Learning Notes (Summarization Project)

---

## 📌 Baseline

* A simple starting method to compare against
* Example: take first 3 sentences of an article
* Used to check if your model is actually better

---

## 📊 ROUGE

* Metric to evaluate summaries
* Compares model summary vs reference summary
* Measures overlap of words/phrases
* Types:

  * ROUGE-1 → words
  * ROUGE-2 → word pairs
  * ROUGE-L → sentence structure similarity

---

## 🤗 Hugging Face

* Platform for ML models and tools
* Provides:

  * pre-trained models
  * datasets
  * evaluation tools (ROUGE, etc.)
* Makes NLP easy to use

---

## 🧠 Fine-tuning

* Taking a pre-trained model and training it on your task
* Goal: improve performance on specific data
* Uses examples (input → output pairs)
* Faster than training from scratch

---

## ⚙️ Training setup terms

### MODEL_NAME

* Base model you start from (e.g. Mistral)

### MAX_SEQ_LEN

* Maximum text the model can read at once

### BATCH_SIZE

* Number of training examples processed together

### GRAD_ACCUM

* Accumulates gradients over multiple batches before updating

### LEARNING_RATE

* How much the model changes each step

### EPOCHS

* Number of times the model sees full dataset

---

## 🧠 Online vs Batch learning

* Online → update after every example ❌
* Batch / mini-batch → update after groups of examples ✅
* Your setup = mini-batch + gradient accumulation

---

## 🧩 LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation)

* Efficient fine-tuning method
* Freezes base model
* Trains small adapter layers only
* Saves memory and compute

---

## ⚙️ LoRA Rank (LORA_RANK)

* Controls the **capacity of the adapter**, not number of adapters
* Example: LORA_RANK = 16 → moderate learning capacity
* NOT “16 adapters”

### Intuition:

* Rank = number of “learning dimensions” inside adapters
* Small rank → fast but limited learning
* Large rank → more powerful but heavier
* 16 = balanced choice

---

## ⚙️ What happens in LoRA training

1. Base model is frozen ❄️
2. Small adapter layers are added 🔧
3. Only adapters are trained 🔥
4. Model learns task-specific behavior

---

## 🔥 Final mental model

* Baseline → simple starting point
* Fine-tuning → teach model task
* LoRA → efficient way to fine-tune
* ROUGE → measure performance
* Hugging Face → tools + models ecosystem
